course: dictionary
lesson: 6364
title: Short forms and what they stand for
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A short form is a word cut down to save time. Msg is short for message. It is an abbreviation, and it has two meanings. In texts and chats, «Send me a msg» means send me a message.
explain: MSG is different. On food labels and in cooking talk, it stands for monosodium glutamate, a salty powder that makes food taste savoury. Context tells you which meaning is right: a phone screen means message, and a food packet means flavour. «Large studies found MSG (a powder added to food to make it taste savoury) safe for most people in normal amounts.»
explain: In school writing, write the full word. Write message, not msg, and write monosodium glutamate the first time you use it. Short forms are fine in quick chats with friends, but they do not belong in an essay.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word, like msg for message.
fact: «msg» (informal, texting) is short for «message».
fact: «MSG» stands for monosodium glutamate, a salty flavour enhancer added to some foods.
fact: Large studies found MSG safe for most people in normal amounts.
fact: Tomatoes and cheese have natural glutamate too.
exercise: «Send me a msg when you get home.» What does msg mean here? | A small game | A type of meal | A kind of bus | *A message
exercise: «Large studies found MSG a powder added to food to make it taste savoury.» What does MSG stand for? | Milk, sugar and ginger | Mixed snack and gravy | *Monosodium glutamate | Most special guest
exercise: You are writing an essay for school. Which word should you write instead of msg? | *message | mess | meal | msg
test: «Some claims you can't test with two seed trays in the kitchen: whether MSG is safe, whether a bridge is sound.» Which question about MSG is mentioned? | Whether it is loud | *Whether it is safe | Whether it is a fruit | Whether it is a colour
test: On a food packet, «no MSG» means the food has | lots of salt and pepper | no sugar at all | *no added monosodium glutamate | no message on the label
exam: «Large studies found MSG safe for most people in normal amounts.» What did the large studies find? | It was dangerous for everyone | *It was safe for most people in normal amounts | It was a kind of bread | Nobody ever tested it
